* Constant-gm (beta-multiplier) self-biased current reference
* Nothing here sets the operating point except the devices themselves: the
* PMOS mirror supplies the NMOS mirror, which supplies the PMOS mirror. The
* cell has a second, degenerate zero-current solution, so a weak resistive
* start-up path breaks it. Rstart is a resistor rather than a long-channel
* MOSFET because the harness renders one geometry per polarity, and a
* minimum-length start-up device would keep conducting in steady state.
* The degeneration branch is two devices in parallel, giving the K=2 width
* ratio the constant-gm relation needs from a single device token.
<MODEL_SETUP>
Vdd vdd 0 <VDD>
Vbn bn 0 <BODY_N>
Vbp bp 0 <BODY_P>
<P_PREFIX>p_mir na nb vdd bp <P_DEVICE>
<P_PREFIX>p_dio nb nb vdd bp <P_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_dio na na 0 bn <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_dega nb na ns bn <N_DEVICE>
<N_PREFIX>n_degb nb na ns bn <N_DEVICE>
Rs ns 0 <BETA_RS>
Rstart vdd na <BETA_RSTART>
<OUTPUT_LOAD>
.temp <TEMP>
<ANALYSIS>
.end
